&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Pinterest:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Millions of people around the world come to our platform to find creative ideas, dream about new possibilities and plan for memories that will last a lifetime. At Pinterest, we’re on a mission to bring everyone the inspiration to create a life they love, and that starts with the people behind the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Discover a career where you ignite innovation for millions, transform passion into growth opportunities, celebrate each other’s unique experiences and embrace the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinterestcareers.com/our-life/pinflex/&quot;&gt;flexibility&lt;/a&gt; to do your best work. Creating a career you love? It’s Possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Pinterest, AI isn&#39;t just a feature, it&#39;s a powerful partner that augments our creativity and amplifies our impact, and we’re looking for candidates who are excited to be a part of that. To get a complete picture of your experience and abilities, we’ll explore your foundational skills and how you collaborate with AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through our interview process, what matters most is that you can always explain your approach, showing us not just what you know, but how you think. You can read more about our AI interview philosophy and how we use AI in our recruiting process &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinterestcareers.com/our-philosophy-on-ai-in-hiring/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pinterest is hiring a Compliance Analyst in Brazil to support our global compliance and ethics program. This person will support and enhance Pinterest’s third party risk management and conflicts of interest programs, day-to-day compliance and employment legal operations, including triage and management of compliance requests, risk assessments, and will support other compliance projects, as needed. The role works closely with the business, Legal, Finance, Procurement, and Corporate Compliance and Ethics leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Third-party risk management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run risk-based due diligence on third parties from onboarding through renewal. Escalate, as needed, to Compliance Leads and Compliance Leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screen third parties against sanctions, watchlists, politically exposed person (PEP) databases, adverse media, and public records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review questionnaires and supporting documents, identify red flags, and recommend risk ratings and mitigation steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross functional partners, like Finance, Procurement and the business, to confirm that diligence is complete and keep records current.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compliance operations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the day-to-day running of the compliance program, including management of intake channels and program and project management, as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain compliance tools, trackers, and dashboards, and prepare regular metrics and reports for compliance leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help review gifts, hospitality, travel, donations, and sponsorships against company policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support monitoring, testing, and audit requests, and track remediation of findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with hotline or speak-up intake and triage as directed, maintaining confidentiality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Development and maintenance of end to end compliance program documentation and supporting continuous improvement of enterprise wide compliance controls and workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate compliance processes for implementation of automation and AI, including working with relevant teams to design work and process flows.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conflicts of interest&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review disclosures, assess potential conflicts, and recommend mitigation plans or escalate to compliance leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep accurate records and follow up with employees and managers until each matter is closed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Projects and advisory&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to and monitor program enhancements, risk assessments, policy updates, and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide practical guidance to local business teams on compliance questions and escalate complex issues appropriately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track changes in regulations, assist with applicability analysis, and the development of requirements and risk and control mapping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support testing of internal controls and audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior corporate compliance experience, ideally in third-party risk, sanctions and export control, anti-corruption, ethics, or conflicts of interest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of anti-corruption frameworks, including U.S. FCPA and similar international laws.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, written, and organizational skills, with sound judgment and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency or professional proficiency in English, as the role works with global teams and documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professionally proficient in AI and automation technologies, including applying them to compliance programs and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrity, discretion, and the ability to handle confidential information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical, business-minded approach to risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication with stakeholders at all levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple workstreams and deadlines independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, with the confidence to escalate and push back when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Law or equivalent. Brazilian bar (OAB) admission is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relocation Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;This position is not eligible for relocation assistance. Visit our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinterestcareers.com/pinflex/&quot;&gt;PinFlex&lt;/a&gt; page to learn more about our working model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;In-Office Requirement Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We recognize that the ideal environment for work is situational and may differ across departments. What this looks like day-to-day can vary based on the needs of each organization or role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will need to be in the office for in-person collaboration at least 1-2 times per week. Therefore needs to be in a commutable distance from &lt;strong&gt;Sao Paulo&lt;/strong&gt; office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
