&lt;p&gt;At Pinterest, AI isn&#39;t just a feature, it&#39;s a powerful partner that augments our creativity and amplifies our impact, and we’re looking for candidates who are excited to be a part of that. To get a complete picture of your experience and abilities, we’ll explore your foundational skills and how you collaborate with AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through our interview process, what matters most is that you can always explain your approach, showing us not just what you know, but how you think. You can read more about our AI interview philosophy and how we use AI in our recruiting process &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinterestcareers.com/our-philosophy-on-ai-in-hiring/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pinterest is seeking a thoughtful, operationally rigorous manager to lead Privacy Operations. This team helps honor people’s privacy rights by managing data subject access requests, deletion requests, PII removals, and underage workflows. The role is based in Dublin and reports to the Privacy Operations leadership team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead day-to-day Privacy Operations performance across request intake, prioritization, service-level commitments, turnaround times, quality, and applicable legal requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use metrics and operating rhythms to forecast demand, manage backlog and capacity, identify risk, and implement mitigations; escalate material issues with clear recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage, coach, and develop full-time Privacy Operations employees through clear goals, 1:1s, feedback, performance management, career development, and inclusive team practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead contingent-workforce execution through clear goals, training, recruiting partnership, and strong vendor relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable onboarding, training, process documentation, and knowledge-management practices for full-time employees, specialists, and contingent teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen operational quality through durable QA, reporting, process controls, and continuous-improvement mechanisms; delegate effectively while retaining accountability for outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a primary operational point of contact for escalations and partner with Legal, the DPO, and cross-functional teams on privacy initiatives that affect operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess the operational impact of policy, regulatory, process, or product changes and drive readiness plans, decisions, and escalations within your remit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to team OKRs and monthly progress reporting, and partner with leadership on short- and long-term strategy, capacity, and operating-model planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI and automation responsibly to improve analysis and operations while protecting sensitive information, validating accuracy, and maintaining ownership of final decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading high-volume, high-judgment operations with service, quality, risk, or regulatory commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience directly managing, coaching, performance-managing, and developing full-time employees; experience leading contingent workforce and/or vendor partners is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use operational data to set priorities, diagnose root causes, communicate risk, and deliver measurable process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment in ambiguous, sensitive, or regulated environments, including knowing when and how to escalate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional communication and partnership skills, including experience working with Legal, Compliance, Policy, Product, Engineering, or similarly complex stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Privacy Operations, Legal Operations, Trust &amp;amp; Safety, Compliance, Customer Operations, or another regulated operational environment. Direct privacy-rights request experience is preferred but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience using AI or automation to improve work, paired with a disciplined approach to data protection, validation, critical thinking, and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
