&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete assigned technical projects with attention to quality, incorporating feedback from your mentor, manager and peers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute scoped technical tasks end-to-end that contribute to Pinterest products and infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver code that is well-documented, tested, and operable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share ideas, questions and perspectives clearly and respectfully while learning from feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build technical and professional skills through learning and development opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with your team and contribute to production-oriented projects that support Pinterest’s goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage opportunities to connect with leaders and colleagues across Pinterest and participate in intern program events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational exposure to AI concepts or AI-assisted software development through coursework, projects, internships or practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in learning how to use AI-powered technologies responsibly to improve product development, while validating outputs through testing, review and engineering judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;:vi&quot; class=&quot;Am aiL Al editable LW-avf tS-tW tS-tY&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently enrolled in a Bachelor’s, Master’s or PhD program in Computer Science, Computer Engineering or a related technical field, with an expected graduation date by June 2028.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated understanding of computer science fundamentals, including data structures and algorithms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience programming in one or more languages such as Java, Python, Go or C++.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with backend development concepts, such as building services or APIs, working with data storage and writing reliable, maintainable code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated work building server-side applications, services or APIs through coursework, internships, hackathons, personal projects, open-source contributions, volunteer work or similar technical work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability using AI to accelerate engineering work while applying judgment to validate accuracy, protect security and know when to ask for help.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in solving complex technical problems and learning in a collaborative engineering environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Office Requirement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This onsite internship will be based in our Zurich office requiring a few days in office. Our program will run in a full-time capacity during typical business hours between Monday-Friday.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will need to be in the office for in-person collaboration 2-3 weekdays per week and therefore needs to be within a commutable distance of &lt;strong&gt;Zurich&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
