&lt;p&gt;Millions of people around the world come to our platform to find creative ideas, dream about new possibilities and plan for memories that will last a lifetime. At Pinterest, we’re on a mission to bring everyone the inspiration to create a life they love, and that starts with the people behind the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Discover a career where you ignite innovation for millions, transform passion into growth opportunities, celebrate each other’s unique experiences and embrace the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinterestcareers.com/our-life/pinflex/&quot;&gt;flexibility&lt;/a&gt; to do your best work. Creating a career you love? It’s Possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Pinterest, AI isn&#39;t just a feature, it&#39;s a powerful partner that augments our creativity and amplifies our impact, and we’re looking for candidates who are excited to be a part of that. To get a complete picture of your experience and abilities, we’ll explore your foundational skills and how you collaborate with AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through our interview process, what matters most is that you can always explain your approach, showing us not just what you know, but how you think. You can read more about our AI interview philosophy and how we use AI in our recruiting process &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinterestcareers.com/our-philosophy-on-ai-in-hiring/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pinterest is looking for a Senior Qualitative Product Researcher (IC15) to shape the future of Search and Home personalization through a deep understanding of how people discover, explore, and return to ideas on Pinterest. In this role, you will lead research on ambiguous, strategically important questions—uncovering people’s goals, intent, and expectations across search and personalized home experiences. Partnering with Product, Design, Engineering, Data Science, and fellow researchers, you will translate these insights into product direction that makes discovery more relevant, useful, and inspiring for each person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and prioritize important user and product questions across a broad problem space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and conduct qualitative research from framing and recruiting through analysis, synthesis, and communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select appropriate research methods and make thoughtful tradeoffs based on the question, timeline, and decision context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize research with existing evidence and partner inputs to develop clear, actionable insights and frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence product strategy, design direction, and prioritization through research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate findings to cross-functional teams and leaders, and help translate insights into decisions and next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to research quality and community through mentorship and knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to quickly onboard emerging AI tools and implement them appropriately in the full product development process with a focus on decision quality, craft and efficiency. Mentors and educates team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in defining, evolving, and applying systems, frameworks, and standards, including using AI-powered tools and workflows to help scale your approach and facilitates productive cross-functional collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 5 years of conducting qualitative user or product research in cross-functional environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong qualitative research toolkit and demonstrated judgment in choosing methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating ambiguous questions into research plans and actionable insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of influencing product or organizational decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, facilitation, and collaboration skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity, self-awareness, sound judgment, and comfort with ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
